<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mir Ali Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mir Ali Bey was an Ottoman corsair who led two expeditions down the East African coast in the 1580s. In 1585–86 he persuaded many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> towns to reject Portuguese overlordship and accept Ottoman protection. On his second expedition in 1588–89 he was besieged at Mombasa by a Portuguese fleet while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimba">Zimba</a> attacked from the mainland, and he was captured and taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>.</p></div>
